Spoilers ahead!

Every experience carries its lesson. In this case, several of them.
Among which:

    1) When you're low on HP, care is good, but sitting quietly (or
       using healing items) is more careful than exploring. Finding 
       a lockable room, a hallway where you can't be attacked from
       all sides, or at least stairs, trapdoor or ^oTele for escape
       makes resting safer, as does having escape items to hand.

    2) Boulder traps are dangerous, but easier to spot than most other
       kinds of trap, since you can often see the boulder. If you do,
       stay off orthogonal lines of movement, approach it, and give it
       a wee shove.

> Now I haven't been playing nethack for long. I just downloaded it a
