Nethack has lots of lethal hazards, and teaches you about them by
killing you. This is in contrast to most commercial games, which take
pains to teach you everything you need beforehand, and make you prove
you know it before demanding you use it in a life-or-death situation.

But, there is hope. Nethack is very fair in that most of the deaths
that seem random or cheap are actually preventable if you can figure
out how.  If you think you died just because the RNG hates you: It
does, but that's not the only reason you died. Reflect on Marvin
winning 12 games out of 13 consecutive, and focus on staying out of
situations where only luck is keeping you alive.

